    "created_at": "2025-09-10T21:33:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-10T21:33:08Z",
    "body": "I agree, using the module script URL is the behavior that makes sense here.\n\nThe right thing to do is probably to have step 5 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-a-css-module-script pass in the options dictionary `{\"baseURL\": script's base URL }`. That'll set the [stylesheet base URL](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-1/#concept-css-style-sheet-stylesheet-base-url), which if present is used over the sheet's [location](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-1/#concept-css-style-sheet-location) in computing the [style resource base URL](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#style-resource-base-url).\n\nI'm not sure if the [location](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-1/#concept-css-style-sheet-location) should be changed. It's reflected in the [`href`](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-1/#dom-stylesheet-href) attribute.  Step 2 of [create a constructed CSSStyleSheet](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#create-a-constructed-cssstylesheet) says it should be set to the \"base URL of the associated Document\", but in my local testing it doesn't look like that's happening. I see `new CSSStyleSheet().href` returning null in Chromium, Firefox, and Safari. Not sure if the spec is wrong there or I'm just missing something.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
